{"ticker":"NTAP","updated":"2026-10-23T23:23:29Z","profile":{"longName":"NetApp, Inc.","shortName":"NetApp, Inc.","sector":"Technology","industry":"Software - Infrastructure","country":"United States","website":"https://www.netapp.com","fullTimeEmployees":11700,"marketCap":42324365312,"trailingPE":30.3921,"forwardPE":19.315722,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":5.7264733,"pegRatio":2.36,"targetMeanPrice":211.6875,"targetHighPrice":300.0,"targetLowPrice":170.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":16,"recommendationKey":"buy","revenueGrowth":0.299,"earningsGrowth":0.635,"grossMargins":0.70625997,"operatingMargins":0.26667,"profitMargins":0.19184999,"totalRevenue":7391000064,"beta":1.45,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":240.87,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":93.69,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NMS","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":0.98},"summary":"NetApp, Inc. develops enterprise software, systems, and services to transform data infrastructures in the United States, Canada, Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the Asia Pacific. It operates through two segments, Hybrid Cloud and Public Cloud. The company offers data management software, such as NetApp ONTAP, ONTAP One, NetApp Snapshot, NetApp SnapCenter Backup Management, NetApp SnapMirror Data Replication, and NetApp SnapLock Data Compliance; and storage infrastructure solutions, including NetApp AFF and ASA A-Series and C-Series, NetApp AFX, NetApp Fabric Attached Storage (FAS), NetApp E/EF series, and NetApp StorageGRID. It also provides cloud storage services comprising Azure NetApp Files, Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP, and Google Cloud NetApp Volumes, as well as NetApp Cloud Volumes ONTAP. In addition, the company offers operational services, such as NetApp Data Infrastructure Insights and Instaclustr; and professional and support services include storage-as-a-service (STaaS), strategic consulting, professional, managed, and support services, as well as assessment, design, implementation, migration, and proactive support services to optimize 